+### What `met=True` does not show (disclosed in the preregistration; wave findings land after the wave)
+
+- C1's mapped check compares the `dev`/`inode` the server's maps line shows with a `stat()` of that pathname and hashes the path now: a file rewritten in place with identical bytes is indistinguishable, and a filesystem whose maps `dev` differs from `stat` `st_dev` (btrfs subvolumes) fails closed; the counter's scratch is xfs. The environment canaries are one variable (`KAMA_R50_CANARY`) and one `PYTHONPATH` `sitecustomize`; `LD_PRELOAD` into the server and a modified `python` on `PATH` are not planted. The teardown leg kills the invoker once, during the hold; kills during download or readiness are not exercised.
+- C2 computes births over every commit reachable from the tip, so a key reborn after deletion adds the rebirth's titles, and text born in both an exempt and a dated section counts as exempt-born (the v4 rule kept). The lane leg bounds the tool's own `ungraded` count by the counter's own v5 count per event, checks `graded + ungraded` and the deletion count against `git diff --numstat`, and keeps the v4 binder copy and the sub-20 threshold.
+- Under the counter's default threshold no integration commit is an event: `tools/append-only-audit.py --to 97c864be --threshold 1` puts the round-49 integration `24e906f0` at `deleted 8 graded 1 ungraded 7 status restored` and the round-48 integration `c4b2175d` at `deleted 8 graded 1 ungraded 7 status restored`, while the default-threshold run has 5 events, all earlier. So the head protocol this round follows — the authority banner appended byte-exact under §Superseded head banners, the exempt head sections re-derived in place — is graded only by the `--threshold 1` run: the one graded line per integration commit is the replaced banner, `restored` only because the old banner is appended byte-exact, and the exempt-born deleted lines are `ungraded` (seven for each of the last two integration commits). That run exits 1 at the build on 60 earlier unrestored sub-20 deletions, which is the debt §Planned (round 51) carries.
